WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.979
All right, I haven't done like a comprehensive
where we are in the pandemic type update for

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:07.759
some time, but it is time to do it.

00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:11.090
A lot of things have changed and there is
much to discuss.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:17.430
So to begin with, we're starting to see some
really significant improvements taking place.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.910
Vaccines are being rolled out more significantly.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.570
I know about the variants.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.580
I know about the so-called mutant strains.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:25.860
And I will talk about them.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.010
I'm not ignoring them.

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.519
I'm aware of them.

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:34.160
I have the latest information as to how they
will affect the vaccination program if this

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.239
or if that.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:36.350
So I'm not ignoring that.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.930
Just give me five minutes to get to it.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:42.230
I know that it's what a lot of folks have
been focused in on, but let's dove right in.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.850
So first of all, cases, just the top line
case number.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:51.040
Back in December, I predicted cases would
peak permanently around January 10th, the

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:52.040
15th.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.040
Now, how did I do this?

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.379
Am I an epidemiologist?

00:00:54.379 --> 00:00:55.379
No.

00:00:55.379 --> 00:00:56.469
Am I a public health expert?

00:00:56.469 --> 00:00:57.469
No.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:00:59.070
Was I special in predicting this?

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.070
No.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.719
Do I want a pat on the back?

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:04.520
Yes, but not for this.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:13.080
A combination of experts were pointing out
that given the winter peak and vaccines being

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:19.820
rolled out and the holiday effect, we were
likely to see a peak sometime around the middle

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:20.860
of January.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:27.210
And case in point case, that's upon the peak
for the seven day case.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:32.900
Average came on January 11th when the United
States hit an average of two hundred and fifty

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.220
five thousand cases per day.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:42.790
Since then, the number of cases has dropped
by more than 40 percent to a seven day case,

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.280
average of one hundred and forty seven thousand
cases.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.760
So the bad news is one hundred and forty seven
thousand new cases a day is insane.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:52.160
It's tragic.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:58.760
It's a disaster being down close to 50 percent
in new cases per day in just a three week

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.120
period.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.010
That is absolutely fantastic.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:06.490
And I expect that by the end of the week we
will be down that full 50 percent.

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:10.610
Now, cases is one thing, but what about deaths?

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:18.090
We also had reason to believe that the death
peak would come three or four weeks after

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.420
the case peak.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.330
Why did we have reason to believe that?

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:27.910
Well, we know from the last year of this pandemic
that deaths lag cases by three to four weeks

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:33.320
and indeed the seven day rolling average of
deaths plateaued over the last seven to 10

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:37.250
days and hopefully, hopefully will be on its
way down soon.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.070
I had thought yesterday or today would be
the peak.

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.610
It turns out we've had sort of a plateau.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:46.070
Let's hope that those death numbers go down
from here still.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:51.890
And I want to be clear that even as we see
things improve, we don't want to forget that

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:56.910
thousands of people have been dying in the
United States every day, 4000 down to three

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.080
thousand is still insane.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.350
It's still a 9/11 every single day.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:03.470
And there is a very long way to go.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:07.660
But the good news is that the numbers are
doing what we thought they would in early

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:12.900
December based on a lot of different factors,
including vaccination.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.830
Let's now talk about that.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:22.930
Officially, the U.S. has seen about 27 million
coronavirus cases and the U.S. has now administered,

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:30.450
not distributed, administered 33 million vaccine
doses into the arms of folks.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:36.050
So we now have officially more doses than
a number of cases.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.050
That's a nice milestone.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:41.990
Now, if you remember my interview with Dr.
Eric Topol a couple of weeks ago, our best

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:46.700
guess right now is that the real number of
cases when you consider that many people never

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:50.590
get tested because they're asymptomatic or
they have mild symptoms and just never going

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:54.860
get a test, the real number of cases is believed
to be somewhere between two and three times

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.700
the official number.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.580
But still, it's a nice thing to be able to
say.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.290
We've now given doses.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:06.380
We've given significantly more doses than
the number of total cases as of right now.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:11.840
As of this morning, eight percent of the US
population has received at least one dose,

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.920
and about two percent of the US population
has received both doses.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:21.549
Remember, with the Pfizer vaccine, you have
twenty one days between dose one and two.

00:04:21.549 --> 00:04:26.090
With the Moderna vaccine, you have twenty
eight days between dose one and two.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.340
You are not considered to be at maximum immunity
potential.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:35.130
And remember, not everybody develops immunity,
but close to 95 percent do.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:41.520
You're not considered to have completed the
full course of vaccination and antibody generation

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:45.890
until seven to 14 days after your second dose?

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:50.520
What we know is that these vaccines are working
really well.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.990
Infections and hospitalizations are down among
those first vaccinated.

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:58.990
This includes health care workers and nursing.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:05.199
Home residents, the two vaccines in play are
Pfizer and Moderna, and although the rollout

00:05:05.199 --> 00:05:10.260
was a little bit slower than we would have
hoped, they are accelerating dramatically.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.520
Pfizer going to bring in additional manufacturers.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.240
A lot is happening there.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:17.320
We also have a third vaccine and more.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.900
But most imminently we have the Johnson and
Johnson vaccine imminently to be submitted

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.210
for approval.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.650
And within a couple of weeks after that, hopefully
emergency use authorization.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.110
That's a one shot vaccine.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:33.560
Now, let's talk about the mutant's, the variants.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:38.730
We have the UK variant, the Brazilian variant
and the South African variant.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:45.660
The concern being vaccines are or might be
less effective against those variants.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:49.130
Some people already going as far as to say
they won't work.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.650
The vaccination program is in vain.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.930
We're vaccinating against the strain that
is not even the strain.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.850
OK, let's stop.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:02.490
Let's sort of break it down a little bit into
its component parts, because much of what

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:04.990
we are being told so far is not true.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:10.230
First of all, the rate at which these I don't
want to call them primary.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:17.030
Yeah, I guess we could call them primary variants
or significant variants are mutating is exactly

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:19.060
as expected for this type of virus.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:23.590
Nothing is happening that was not predictable
in terms of these types of viruses and mutation.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.160
That's number one.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:33.120
Number two, the as close as we can currently
get to a reality based assessment of the effectiveness

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.060
of vaccines on the variance is as follows.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:43.570
The two vaccines currently in use, Fizer and
Moderna, in the United States appear to be

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:50.810
essentially as effective against the UK variant
and the Brazilian variant as they are against

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:54.470
the sort of main strain as we might know it.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:07:01.440
It is true that the antibodies generated by
these vaccines appear to be less effective

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.020
against the South African variant.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:10.740
That doesn't mean that they don't still generate
enough antibodies to be immune for most people

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.400
against the South African variant.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.560
And what I mean by that is as follows.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:18.910
When you vaccinate people, they generate antibodies
on a curve.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:24.110
And, you know, we talk about it's 95 percent
effective.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:29.400
What we mean by that is five percent of people
who get the vaccine don't generate enough

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.020
antibodies for immunity.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:36.050
Now, you might still generate enough to avoid
a hospitalization or a death, but five percent

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:40.330
don't generate enough antibodies for immunity
to the primary strain.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:45.500
But you have a curve, so you might have just
sign fake numbers to it.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:52.560
95 percent of people generate at least a 100
level of antibodies, 90 percent generate at

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:58.880
least 200 level of antibodies, 80 percent
or at the thousand level, so on and so forth.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:04.970
While it appears to be true that the antibodies
generated are less effective against the South

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:10.940
African variant, it may still be effective
enough for most people to be immune.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:18.500
Imagine that the antibodies generated are
a thousand level and only 100 of them are

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:21.080
effective against the South African variant.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.979
Well, if the threshold to be immune is only
ninety five, then you're still OK and I hope

00:08:25.979 --> 00:08:27.520
I'm being clear about that.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.410
So we still are gathering information about
this.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:37.069
The idea that the vaccines don't work against
the variance so far is not based in fact,

00:08:37.069 --> 00:08:38.069
or science.

00:08:38.069 --> 00:08:39.289
It's not yet been demonstrated.

00:08:39.289 --> 00:08:42.079
And importantly, this is a race against the
variants.

00:08:42.079 --> 00:08:47.130
The variants are a reason to vaccinate as
quickly as possible, not to delay vaccination.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.839
Viruses mutate by spreading.

00:08:48.839 --> 00:08:54.260
The more people that vaccinate more quickly,
we slow the spread of the variants and prevent

00:08:54.260 --> 00:09:00.100
more people from getting that variant, which
may be a less controlled by the vaccines.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:07.410
We currently have Moderna and Fizer both working
on a sort of modified booster in case it is

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.980
necessary for some period down the road.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.240
Could be eight or 12 months from now or maybe
even longer now.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:17.600
As I said on the bonus show, I was on a wait
list for leftover doses.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:22.730
A lot of of of hospitals and vaccination facilities
are having issues where because there's multiple

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:27.949
doses in a vial, you might get to the end
of the day and have leftover doses.

00:09:27.949 --> 00:09:30.939
And most hospitals have some kind of on call
list.

00:09:30.939 --> 00:09:32.879
I have a friend who works at a hospital.

00:09:32.879 --> 00:09:33.980
I said, put me on the list.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:37.550
I will give me 30 minutes notice and I will
show up.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:42.629
We you know, she doesn't want any doses going
to waste, and neither do I. I was able over

00:09:42.629 --> 00:09:46.300
the weekend to get the first dose of the Moderna
vaccine.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:49.230
I had more arm pain being a lefty.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:54.010
I got it in my right arm, more arm pain than
for any vaccine I've had in my life.

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:58.649
I had a fever and flu like symptoms for about
twenty four thirty hours.

00:09:58.649 --> 00:10:04.769
I spent Saturday in bed, I am now feeling
fine and I'm ready and waiting for my second

00:10:04.769 --> 00:10:06.269
dose in a few weeks.

00:10:06.269 --> 00:10:08.239
Now, one last thing I want to talk about.

00:10:08.239 --> 00:10:14.499
There are more and more articles being written
expressing concern that these vaccines are

00:10:14.499 --> 00:10:17.009
being undersold and they're being undersold.

00:10:17.009 --> 00:10:23.201
When you hear cautious public health experts
say things like even after vaccinated, you

00:10:23.201 --> 00:10:28.119
still should social distance and wear masks
and avoid indoor crowds and all of this different

00:10:28.119 --> 00:10:29.230
stuff.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:35.619
And I think it's important to understand that
until we reach a level approaching herd immunity,

00:10:35.619 --> 00:10:39.930
we all still need to continue taking a number
of the precautions that many of us have been

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:40.939
taking.

00:10:40.939 --> 00:10:45.360
But we don't want to undersell the importance
of the vaccine because then you're going to

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:50.589
see a lot of people say what they are saying
now, which is even if I get the vaccine, nothing

00:10:50.589 --> 00:10:51.589
changes.

00:10:51.589 --> 00:10:53.430
Well, then I'm just not going to get the vaccine.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:58.149
The truth is that these vaccines, particularly
Pfizer and Moderna, are almost 100 percent

00:10:58.149 --> 00:11:00.790
effective at preventing death or even serious
covid.

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.800
That is a huge game changer.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:09.929
While it has not yet been confirmed that the
vaccinated individuals spread the disease

00:11:09.929 --> 00:11:13.420
to a significantly lesser degree, that's what
would be expected.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.209
And that's usually how vaccines work.

00:11:15.209 --> 00:11:19.350
So I am a little worried about the degree
to which the vaccines are undersold.

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:25.589
As I said on the bonus show, and as I've spoken
about with, you know, public health officials

00:11:25.589 --> 00:11:31.379
and epidemiologists who are speaking not for
the media, but just kind of between people

00:11:31.379 --> 00:11:39.730
in six weeks, in eight weeks, a group of four
or six vaccinated people who work from home

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:43.879
are able to be together with extremely low
risk.

00:11:43.879 --> 00:11:45.970
It is not zero.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.649
Nothing is ever zero.

00:11:47.649 --> 00:11:52.240
But these vaccines are game changers and we
want to make sure we are not underselling

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.699
them and we continue vaccinating as quickly
as possible.

00:11:55.699 --> 00:12:01.149
I get people are being cautious, but if we
start telling people, even with vaccination,

00:12:01.149 --> 00:12:03.139
you still have to social distance and wear
masks.

00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:07.709
And definitely a lot of people will say, well,
I'm going to opt out and we don't want that.

00:12:07.709 --> 00:12:08.709
Send me your thoughts.

00:12:08.709 --> 00:12:11.059
I am on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:12:11.059 --> 00:12:12.779
This is good news.

00:12:12.779 --> 00:12:15.980
Notice I didn't mention Trump or Biden in
this entire segment.

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:19.690
This is an analysis of the data and the science
of what is going on.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:23.019
This is not a political statement, a political
segment of any kind.

00:12:23.019 --> 00:13:48.069
Let me know your thoughts.

